Z||000012||Monkeyman||11-26-2001||03:57 AM||||yo_sweet--Are you sure you know which version of the Supra we're talking about?  The MkIV looks very importish/ricey/"Jap car", but the Mk III doesn't.  Here's a pic of a Mk III.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Black_Supra_1.jpg">  <BR>Just making sure you weren't thinking of a MkIV like this.  (BTW-This MkIV has a Veilside body kit.  This is not a stock body.)<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SupraVeilside.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Mr.Frosty||11-26-2001||11:50 AM||||Correct me if I'm wrong,but I thought the Mk.1's were the boxy Celica "Supra" of the early 80's the Mk.2's were like the first black one Monkeyman posted,and the Mk.3's were the big bulgy curvy ones.Like the last one you posted and like the one in Fast and Furious? If I'm wrong ,which model did I miss?<P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled||||reg||1
Z||000014||btoth||11-26-2001||12:11 PM||||Yeah, I thought the mid '90s Supras were the 3rd generation.  I love the tail lights and the interior of the last ones.  Feels just like a cockpit.||||reg||7
Z||000015||Monkeyman||11-26-2001||05:58 PM||||The MkIIs were the Celica variation.  (Basically just a stretched Celica.)  The MkIIIs all looked the same other than some subtle trim differences.  (First pic.)  The Mk IVs are the last generation.  (Second pic.)  Very smooth and curvy.  Those were the 320hp twin turbo cars.  Very fast (and very expensive).  Mk IIs were produced up though '86, MkIIIs were from '86.5 to '92 and the MkIVs were produced from '93 through '98.  There is a rumor going around that Toyota will produce a MkV in the next few years.  I've always thought that the MkIVs looked generic and ricey, even in stock trim.  The MkIIIs look muscular.||||reg||1
